Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] FunctionOpInterface: the signature edits are interface methods

`insertArguments`, `insertResults`, `eraseArguments` and `eraseResults`
are shared class declarations of `FunctionOpInterface`, so the copy in
the interface class runs whatever the operation is: a caller holding a
`FunctionOpInterface` never reaches an operation's own version, and an
operation that keeps facts tied to the positions of its arguments or
results (an attribute per argument, say) cannot keep them in step under
a generic caller, since none of the hooks the edits call is given the
indices.

The four edits become interface methods whose default implementations
are the present bodies, so every operation that does not override them
behaves as before. The single-item forms (`insertArgument`,
`insertResult`, `eraseArgument`, `eraseResult`) call the edit through
the operation, so they reach an override too.

Test: `test.positional_func` overrides the four edits to keep a tag per
argument and result, which its verifier checks; the `test-func-*`
passes, which edit through the interface, keep the tags in step.
